{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["And the reason for <b>and you shall bless me also</b> — as you slaughter to YHWH your Elohim as you have spoken, and you pray for your own lives that no plague or sword strike you, you shall mention me as well along with you. And Rashi said: pray for me that I do not die, for I am a firstborn. But its plain sense is that they should bless him and his kingdom, for the blessing of the king includes the peace of the entire kingdom. And in the Mekhilta (here): pray for me that the punishment cease from me, meaning that he not be punished any further on their account."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:13.849760638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}